request.description:
There is no `/api/hiring-rounds` create endpoint in the current implementation. Run once (single-quoted --execute, double-quoted PHP strings -- no backslash-escaping needed, safe to copy straight out of this description):

  docker compose exec laravel php artisan tinker --execute='
  $admin = App\Models\User::where("email", "admin@mcdss.local")->first();
  $round = App\Models\HiringRound::firstOrCreate(
      ["name" => "Phase 8 Test Round"],
      ["semester" => "Phase8-Semester", "academic_year" => 2026, "start_date" => "2026-11-01", "end_date" => "2027-03-31", "status" => "active", "created_by" => $admin?->id]
  );
  echo $round->id;
  '

Paste the echoed UUID into the 'phase8_round_id' collection variable. This round's start_date (2026-11-01) is later than the seeded round's (2026-06-01), so it becomes the 'currently active' round that POST /api/applications auto-attaches to -- meaning it's safe to close in Section 2 without affecting the shared seeded round other collections depend on.

Run once (single-quoted --execute, double-quoted PHP strings):

  docker compose exec laravel php artisan tinker --execute='
  $admin = App\Models\User::where("email", "admin@mcdss.local")->first();
  $round = App\Models\HiringRound::firstOrCreate(
      ["name" => "Phase 8 Test Round 2 (Zero Unhired Regression)"],
      ["semester" => "Phase8-Semester-2", "academic_year" => 2026, "start_date" => "2026-12-01", "end_date" => "2027-04-30", "status" => "active", "created_by" => $admin?->id]
  );
  echo $round->id;
  '

Paste the echoed UUID into the 'round2_id' collection variable. Its start_date (2026-12-01) is later than 'Phase 8 Test Round', so it becomes the new auto-attach target for POST /api/applications from here on.
